%% Sequence diagram for Scenario 4: Kubernetes Fault Tolerance & Rerouting
%%
%% Render to PNG with:
%%   npx -y @mermaid-js/mermaid-cli@11 -i docs/sequence-diagram-scenario4.mmd \
%%       -o docs/sequence-diagram-scenario4.png -b white -s 3
%%
%% Or paste the code below into https://mermaid.live and export the PNG.

sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Users as End Users
    participant GW as Level 1: API Gateway
    participant LB as Load Balancer
    participant SV as Surviving Replicas 1 and 2
    participant R3 as Replica 3 on Node C
    participant NR as Replacement Replica
    participant KCP as Kubernetes Control Plane
    participant JG as OpenTelemetry, Jaeger and AI

    Note over Users,R3: PHASE 0 - HEALTHY BASELINE (42 requests per second)
    Users->>GW: Continuous order requests
    GW->>LB: Forward request
    LB->>SV: Two thirds of traffic
    LB->>R3: One third of traffic
    R3-->>GW: 200 OK (about 110 ms)
    GW->>JG: Trace: HEALTHY (records serving pod and node)

    Note over R3: FAULT INJECTED - Node C is killed instantly

    Note over Users,KCP: PHASE 1 - BLACK HOLE (about 40 s)
    Users->>GW: Requests continue
    GW->>LB: Forward request
    LB--xR3: One third of traffic still sent to the dead replica
    R3--xGW: No response - Gateway gives up after 5 s
    GW->>JG: Trace: ERROR (upstream timeout)
    Note right of GW: Failures spike, but the surviving path stays fast
    KCP->>LB: Node C missed its heartbeats - remove it from the endpoints

    Note over Users,SV: PHASE 2 - BROWNOUT (two replicas carry all the load)
    Users->>GW: Requests continue
    GW->>LB: Forward request
    LB->>SV: All of the traffic
    SV-->>GW: 200 OK but slow - queue grows to about 1900 ms
    GW->>JG: Trace: HEALTHY but heavily degraded latency
    Note right of LB: No failures now, but roughly 15 times slower

    Note over KCP,NR: PHASE 3 - RECOVERY
    KCP->>NR: Schedule a replacement replica on a surviving node
    Note right of NR: Not usable yet - 15 s warm-up
    NR->>LB: Readiness probe passes - added to the endpoints
    LB->>NR: Traffic resumes across three replicas
    NR-->>GW: 200 OK - backlog drains, latency returns to baseline
    GW->>JG: Trace: HEALTHY (back to about 110 ms)

    Note over JG: DATA PIPELINE AND PREDICTION
    JG->>JG: Flatten traces to one row per second and label each second
    JG->>Users: "Node failure detected. Estimated time to full restabilization: 124 s"
